  "track.runtime.m.snapshot.title": "Writing state, applying and invalidating",
  "track.runtime.m.snapshot.overview": "`count` is a `mutableStateOf(0)`. Choose whether to write inside a mutable snapshot or directly, and whether any scope reads `count`.",
  "track.runtime.m.snapshot.wrapup": "Reading state records who depends on it; writing it creates a change; when the change is applied, only the scopes that read that state are invalidated. If nobody reads it, there is nothing to recompose.",
  "track.runtime.m.snapshot.simp.1": "The model does not draw StateRecords. A state object can have several records for several snapshots; that is a concept, not a memory layout described here.",
  "track.runtime.m.snapshot.simp.2": "Apply conflicts are only mentioned, not simulated.",
  "track.runtime.m.snapshot.ctl.hint": "Two switches: where the write happens and whether anyone reads the state.",
  "track.runtime.m.snapshot.ctl.isolated": "Write inside a mutable snapshot",
  "track.runtime.m.snapshot.ctl.read": "Text reads count",
  "track.runtime.m.snapshot.diagramTitle": "Runtime diagram: Snapshot and Recomposer",
  "track.runtime.m.snapshot.diagramDesc": "Snapshot notifies the Recomposer, which asks the Composition to run again.",
  "track.runtime.m.snapshot.s.read.title": "The read is recorded",
