  "track.runtime.m.focus.s.intro.plain.title": "A plain Row",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.s.intro.plain.explain": "No merging modifier: every element with semantics is its own node.",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.ev.intro.plain": "A plain Row",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.s.intro.merge.title": "A Row with clickable",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.s.intro.merge.explain": "The whole row opens the article when tapped. `clickable` brings a semantics modifier that merges descendants.",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.ev.intro.merge": "A Row with clickable",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.s.intro.clear.title": "A clickable Row plus customActions",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.s.intro.clear.explain": "As in the Android docs on merging: the bookmark button is under `clearAndSetSemantics { }`, and its action moves up to the Row as a custom action.",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.ev.intro.clear": "A clickable Row plus customActions",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.s.tree.plain.title": "The unmerged tree: 5 nodes",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.s.tree.plain.explain": "The thumbnail (contentDescription), two Texts, the IconButton (role Button, onClick) and the icon inside it.",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.ev.tree.plain": "The unmerged tree: 5 nodes",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.s.tree.merge.title": "The unmerged tree: 6 nodes",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.s.tree.merge.explain": "Plus the Row's node (with onClick and the merge flag). The unmerged tree keeps every node; merging is up to whoever reads the tree.",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.ev.tree.merge": "The unmerged tree: 6 nodes",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.s.tree.clear.title": "The unmerged tree: 4 nodes",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.s.tree.clear.explain": "The bookmark button and its icon vanish from the tree: `clearAndSetSemantics { }` with an empty lambda erases its own and its descendants' semantics. The Row gains the \"Add to bookmarks\" custom action.",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.ev.tree.clear": "The unmerged tree: 4 nodes",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.s.rule.plain.title": "Nothing to merge",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.s.rule.plain.explain": "No node sets `mergeDescendants` except the IconButton (merging its own icon).",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.ev.rule.plain": "Nothing to merge",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.s.rule.merge.title": "Merging: the thumbnail and two Texts into the Row; the button stays apart",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.s.rule.merge.explain": "Each property has its own merge policy; contentDescription and text, for example, are collected into lists. But a parent cannot merge children that merge THEMSELVES: the IconButton is clickable, so it is not merged into the Row.",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.ev.rule.merge": "Merging: the thumbnail and two Texts into the Row; the button stays apart",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.s.rule.clear.title": "Merging the rest into the Row",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.s.rule.clear.explain": "The thumbnail and two Texts merge into the Row as before; the button has been erased, so nothing stands apart.",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.ev.rule.clear": "Merging the rest into the Row",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.s.walk.plain.title": "TalkBack stops {n} times for one row",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.s.walk.plain.explain": "The user must swipe through the thumbnail, the title, the metadata and the button for EVERY article. Every list of posts hits exactly this.",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.ev.walk.plain": "TalkBack stops {n} times for one row",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.s.walk.merge.title": "TalkBack stops {n} times",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.s.walk.merge.explain": "Once for the whole row (reading the thumbnail, title and metadata together), once for the bookmark button.",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.ev.walk.merge": "TalkBack stops {n} times",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.s.walk.clear.title": "TalkBack stops {n} time",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.s.walk.clear.explain": "One stop for the whole row; \"Add to bookmarks\" lives in TalkBack's actions menu.",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.ev.walk.clear": "TalkBack stops {n} time",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.s.find.plain.title": "The test finds the Text itself",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.s.find.plain.explain": "`onNodeWithText(\"Compose phases\")` uses the merged tree by default; nothing merges, so the node is the Text.",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.ev.find.plain": "The test finds the Text itself",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.s.find.merge.title": "The test finds the merged Row node",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.s.find.merge.explain": "In the merged tree, the two Texts' text lives in the Row node, so the finder returns the Row. To get the Text node itself, pass `useUnmergedTree = true`.",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.ev.find.merge": "The test finds the merged Row node",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.s.find.clear.title": "The test finds the merged Row node",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.s.find.clear.explain": "As in the merged version. Note: the bookmark button is gone from the tree, so tests cannot find it either; test it through the custom action.",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.ev.find.clear": "The test finds the merged Row node",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.s.end.plain.title": "The end: correct, but tiring for TalkBack users",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.s.end.plain.explain": "All the information is there, but split too finely.",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.ev.end.plain": "The end: correct, but tiring for TalkBack users",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.s.end.merge.title": "The end: one row, one button",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.s.end.merge.explain": "A sensible granularity for most lists.",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.ev.end.merge": "The end: one row, one button",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.s.end.clear.title": "The end: one stop, one custom action",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.s.end.clear.explain": "The fastest way to skim a list, at the price of declaring everything by hand.",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.ev.end.clear": "The end: one stop, one custom action",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.co.rule.plain": "The docs: a composable with no semantics properties set is not part of the semantics tree. [[src:cp-semantics]]",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.co.rule.merge": "The Android docs say: a parent cannot merge its children when the children are also merging, through `mergeDescendants = true` or by being buttons or clickables. [[src:cp-merging]]",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.co.rule.clear": "The Android docs say: modifier order matters; `clearAndSetSemantics` clears all semantics after where it is applied, regardless of merging. [[src:cp-merging]]",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.co.find": "Finders and matchers use the merged tree by default; `useUnmergedTree = true` switches to the unmerged tree. [[src:cp-semantics]] [[src:cp-testing-apis]]",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.co.end.plain": "The fix: group a post's actions into custom actions for faster skimming. [[src:book-compose-tut]]",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.co.end.merge": "`clickable`, `toggleable` and `ListItem` merge their descendants automatically. [[src:cp-semantics]]",
  "track.runtime.m.focus.co.end.clear": "The docs: services receive no information when this API is set, so use it sparingly; semantics may also be used by AI agents to understand the screen. [[src:cp-merging]]",
  "track.runtime.cap.focus": "Left to right: ArticleRow's UI tree produces the semantics tree; top right is TalkBack (reading the unmerged tree and merging itself), bottom right is the testing framework (reading the merged tree by default). The metrics count unmerged nodes, TalkBack stops and custom actions.",
  "track.runtime.b9.sim.runtime.focus": "Merging, clearing and stops",
